  "name": "Question 15",
  "problem": "Given that $P(B)=\\frac{1}{2},$ $P(A\\cap B)=\\frac{1}{4},$ and $P(A\\cup B)=\\frac{2}{3},$ find $P({A}^{\u2032}).$",
  "worked_solution": "First, we calculate $P(A)$ using the addition law:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(A\\cup B) & =P(A)+P(B)-P(A\\cap B) \\\\ \\frac{2}{3} & =P(A)+\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ P(A) & =\\frac{2}{3}+\\frac{1}{4}-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ P(A) & =\\frac{5}{12}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P({A}^{\u2032}) & =1-P(A) \\\\  & =1-\\frac{5}{12} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{12}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
